course: dictionary
lesson: 9648
title: Plates that dive
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: The Earth's outer shell is cut into big pieces called tectonic plates, and they move very slowly. You do not need to know every word to understand a text. Read the words around a new word, because they are its context. «Where an ocean plate meets another plate, the denser one dives down in a subduction zone, making a deep trench and a line of volcanoes.»
explain: The clues are dives down, deep trench and line of volcanoes. So subduction is the process where one plate slides down under another. Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "the denser one slides under, in a place where one plate sinks under another" still makes sense.
explain: A subduction zone is the place where this happens. Subduction is a noun for the process, and in a subduction zone it is the adjective-like word that tells you which place you mean. The sinking plate goes down into the hot mantle, below the Earth's crust.
fact: Subduction means one tectonic plate slides under another and sinks into the hot mantle.
fact: A subduction zone is the place where this happens.
fact: Subduction zones can make deep ocean trenches, volcanoes and big earthquakes.
fact: The Mariana Trench, the deepest place in the ocean, formed by subduction.
fact: The Pacific "Ring of Fire" is full of subduction zones, near Japan, Chile, Alaska and New Zealand.
exercise: Read «Where an ocean plate meets another plate, the denser one dives down in a subduction zone, making a deep trench and a line of volcanoes.» What does subduction mean? | A plate breaks off and floats into space | Two plates slide sideways past each other and never sink | *One plate slides down under another and sinks into the hot mantle | A volcano erupts from the ocean floor
exercise: In the same sentence, what dives down? | The trench | The mantle | The volcano | *The denser plate
exercise: The Pacific "Ring of Fire" is full of what? | *Subduction zones | Desert plains | Coral reefs | Flat ice sheets
test: Which feature was formed by subduction and is the deepest place in the ocean? | The Sahara Desert | Mount Everest | *The Mariana Trench | Lake Victoria
test: Which of these can subduction zones cause? | *Volcanoes and deep ocean trenches | Rainbows over the sea | Pink sand beaches | Snow on the equator
exam: Why does a line of volcanoes often appear near a subduction zone? | Rain washes lava down the mountains | The plates are sliding sideways and rubbing | *The sinking plate heats and melts rock, which can rise up and erupt | Ice on the ocean floor cracks open
